  "identifier": "invesalius",
  "name": "InVesalius",
  "description": "Open-source 3D medical image reconstruction software that generates volumetric models from 2D DICOM slices (CT and MRI). Features segmentation tools, surface mesh export (STL, OBJ, PLY, VRML) for 3D printing and surgical planning, volume rendering, and measurement tools. Developed and maintained by CTI Renato Archer, a Brazilian federal research institution under the Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovations. Widely used for surgical simulation, prosthetics planning, and biomedical research. GPL-2.0, Python/Rust, 785 stars, 433 forks, v3.1.99998 (April 2024). Available in 10 languages.",
  "url": "https://invesalius.github.io/",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/invesalius/invesalius3",
  "license": "GPL-2.0-only",
  "version": "3.1.99998",
